  "tagline": "AWS's serverless ledger database with a cryptographically verifiable journal, retired in July 2025.",
  "description": "Amazon Quantum Ledger Database was a fully managed ledger service: an immutable, append-only journal hashed into a verifiable chain, with documents in Amazon Ion queried through PartiQL, built-in history views and journal streaming to Kinesis. It targeted systems of record that need a trustworthy change history without running a blockchain. AWS announced its retirement in 2024 and ended support on 31 July 2025, and directed customers to Aurora PostgreSQL with audit extensions. It is listed here for migration context only.",
